ading","level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"N · tr(L_g⁻¹) − 1ᵀ L_g⁻¹ 1 with L_g the Laplacian grounded at the vertex of largest degree,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from its GTH elimination (as ","type":"text"},{"code":"numberOfSpanningTrees","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"): every term is a sum of positive ones,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so the result keeps a relative accuracy of about n² · 10⁻¹⁶ under any weight spread, where","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"n · Σ 1\/λᵢ over a dense spectrum loses it. O(n³) time, n² ","type":"text"},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/effectiveGraphResistance()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph\/effectivegraphresistance()"]}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory/GraphProtocols/Graph/effectiveGraphResistance()":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The effective graph resistance (the Kirchhoff index of Klein and Randić): the sum of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"resistanceDistance"},{"type":"text","text":" over unordered pairs of vertices, n · Σ_{i≥2} 1\/λᵢ over the Laplacian"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"spectrum; nil when the graph is not connected, 0 for zero or one vertex. NetworkX"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"effective_graph_resistance"},{"type":"text","text":" (which returns ∞ when disconnected)."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"effectiveGraphResistance